{
 "notes": ["Wild Machines' used SVs (original scene 15, state 3: setup 0x27607 and 0x1ee3d, input 0x27910, draws 0x230f4 and 0x2022b; trade 0x268c0 and 0x2605f, hangars 0x25126 and 0x203bd, notices 0x27ae2). Opened from the Wild Machines menu (data/ui/wild_machines.json), which it goes back to. layers: the list at 0x1dd090 (0xbbc3d): the background (2958), the BUY SV banner (2960) at the top and the CURRENT MUSIC band (2959) at y 376, both on layer 0x101.", "The lineup is the calendar day's used_svs (tables/garage.json used_sv_lineups, 0x252ee8: up to six robot records); SVs whose body's maker is from_maker (Tolomeo) on show only once contest 49 is won (0x5f750, 0x96f64). The price is the SV's parts added up (0x392ff). With fewer than six the last slots are used.", "opening: the strip (3021) fades in over 20 frames, then shop_open (sys 44) plays and the USED-SV plate (3032) slides in from x -400, 20 a frame; the SVs take input once it is in. The icons slide in meanwhile, 20 a frame, each from its slide_from (x - 1220 + 60 a slot). The three gears turn together, 0.01 radians a frame.", "slots: each SV's icon is its legs' (0x1dd170: the lit sprite, the plain one the sprite before it), EXIT 2976/2977; the chosen one is lit over its plain one. left/right move (sys 3); confirm (sys 5) opens the trade window or goes back; cancel jumps to EXIT (sys 4).", "info: over an SV the panel (3022) grows open over 10 frames and shrinks on EXIT; once open it shows the maker's badge (0x1dd06c by the body's maker: Holy, Photon, Aeron, Tolomeo, Tolomeo R, Charga), the SV's name and the price. The original centres the panel on (200, 244) and the gears on their positions. The SV under the cursor stands turning on the right (0x22612 loads it, 0x226c6 shows it once loaded, 0x836b8 swaps it in), in Wild Machines' preview (mode 3, 0x026d86: data/ui/robot_preview.json's module_shop, sliding in from the right); none over EXIT.", "trade: SV SPEC, BUY, CANCEL on the window (2962), the chosen label (0x1dd438) orange and pulsing. SV SPEC opens its spec screen (0x10f5c), which comes back here. BUY checks the money (poor), the stock (no_stock) and an empty hangar of the player's (no_hangar), then the hangars.", "hangars: the carousel (2974, numbers 0x1dd48c) scrolls 60 a step over 8 frames; confirm on one that does not fit says in_use or not_yours, otherwise pays, fits the SV with its CHIP named after its record (sys 27) and says delivered, then asks to board it (0x25741); boarding says boarded; either way name_chip leads to NAME ENTRY for the CHIP (0x2c5d9 mode 2), which comes back here. B CANCEL (0x6ded3) goes back to the trade window (sys 8).", "The help lines (0x1dce74, 0x1dce7c, 0x1dce88) scroll at y 72 with 40 leading spaces (the lead, 9 units a space)."],
